      "title": "Sand settles, mud overflows",
      "description": "Coarse sand (typically > ~ 100 µm) settles quickly in the pool and is raked up the incline, draining and being washed on the way, while fine red mud stays in suspension and overflows the weir to the washers. Removing sand early reduces erosion in thickeners, pumps and pipelines; the washed sand is often used for residue-area construction.",
